        {
          "id": 1780129451,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Thanks for reviewing my change.\n\nBut... I don't quite follow your suggestion.  I need to clear the column so that I have empty space to start appending into.  The `\"Telnet Data...\"` string is now only used as a fallback for in case nothing else was put into the column.  Are you saying I should clear the column with `col_set_str(pinfo->cinfo, COL_INFO, \"\")` to avoid the need to check `col_get_writable` later?  I will still need to use `strlen` (or some other check) to see whether anything has been put in the column during the dissection.\n\nOr I guess I could leave `\"Telnet Data...\"` in the column initially, add tracking of the number of items dissected, use `col_set_xxx` when the first item is added, and `col_append_xxx` for subsequent entries... which would also eliminate the problem of a possible packet containing a large number of entries producing excessively long text here.  It would also eliminate the possibility of a blank column if an exception occurs.  Hmmmm.  I might try this approach.",
