        {
          "id": 1780195556,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Right, I was thinking about avoiding the blank column if an exception occurs. It's a little annoying bookkeeping either way, to be sure.\n\n> col_set_xxx when the first item is added, \n\nImportantly, this has to be `col_add_[fl]str` if the added string is not a static `const char*` but is instead dynamically allocated. `col_add_str` copies. (For that reason there aren't `col_set_[fl]str`, so I'm sure you would have figured it out. It does occasionally cause issues, though.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
